# Flask assistant

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.6+-blue.svg)
![Flask](https://img.shields.io/badge/Flask-1.1.1-blue.svg)
![SQLite](https://img.shields.io/badge/SQLite-3.31.1-blue.svg)
![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-20.10.0-blue.svg)

This is a simple assistant that allows you to run a Flask app in a container.

## Requirements

* [Python](https://www.python.org/) 3.6+
* [Docker](https://www.docker.com/) 20.10.0+

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/mariellange/flask-assistant.git
cd flask-assistant
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Usage

```bash
FLASK_ENV=development FLASK_APP=app.py flask run
```

## License

[MIT](https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/)
