---
title: Binary Search
categories: [algorithms, implementation]
---

Binary search is a divide and conquer algorithm that takes in 1 sorted array and returns the index of the element if it exists. If the element doesn't exist, it returns -1.

Binary search is faster than linear search as it reduces the search space by half every iteration.


## Implementation

```java
public int binary_search(int[] arr, int element) {
    int low = 0;
    int high = arr.length - 1;
    while (low <= high) {
        int mid = (low + high) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == element) {
            return mid;
        } else if (element < arr[mid]) {
            high = mid - 1;
        } else {
            low = mid + 1;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
```

## Complexity

* Time: O(log n)
* Space: O(1)
